johnwalbright@aol.com (JohnWAlbright) writes:

> could give me some tips on  surviving. Problems I've had thus far are:
> Food Poisoning

Don't eat old corpses. If it's been dead for longer than about 50 turns,
it's probably tainted. If you didn't just kill it or see it get killed, it
is probably older than 50 turns.
(Notice that if you begin eating something and get interrupted, you can
count the turns starting from when you got interrupted. So, it's ok to
bite something, get interrupted, wait for another 40 turns, start eating
and get interrupted, wait for another 40 turns and so on.)
Lizard, lichen and acid blob corpses are an exception, they never get
tainted. And undead corpses (zombie, vampire) are always considered old.

> Gnomish Mines (great place to get some good equipment but usually too
> tough)

Don't get surrounded. Try to do the fighting in narrow corridors. Retreat
to heal if you get low on Hp, and come back when you are better.

> Wererats (lycanthropy stinks)

Don't let them come near you if you can avoid it. Use ranged attacks:
throw daggers and darts, zap wands. If you get lycanthropy, eating a sprig
of wolfsbane or quaffing holy water will cure it. Also, you may #pray for
your god to help, if it's been long enough since you last prayed or
received a gift and have not done anything to piss off the god.

> running out of food

Eat corpses. Most of them are edible, but not all. Remembering what I
wrote about old corpses, you should soon be able to learn which are edible
and which are not.

> generally running into monster that kick my butt and ruin all my fun.

You don't need to kill everything as soon as you see them. Run away when
low on Hp.

